course: dictionary
lesson: 15309
title: Slippy and slippery
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slippy is an informal word, used most in the UK, Ireland and Australia. It means slippery: smooth or wet, so that you slide or fall easily. «Careful, it's slippy!» is a warning to watch your step.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The path was slippy after the rain.» Rain makes things wet, and wet things are slippy, so the rain tells you what the word means.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in a meaning. "The path was slippery after the rain" still makes sense, so slippy means slippery. Slippy is often used in phrases like slippy floor and slippy road.
explain: In school stories and formal writing, people usually write slippery instead of slippy. You will still hear slippy in everyday talk, so it helps to know both.
fact: Slippy means slippery: smooth or wet, so that you slide or fall easily.
fact: Slippy is an informal word, mostly used in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: «Careful, it's slippy!» is a warning about icy paths or wet floors.
fact: Slippy can be used in phrases like «slippy floor» and «slippy road».
fact: Slippy and slippery mean the same thing, but slippery is the more formal word.
exercise: «Careful, the path is slippy after the rain.» What does slippy mean? | *Smooth or wet, so you slide easily | Tall and thin | Dry and warm in the sun | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «The kitchen floor was slippy, so Sam walked very slowly.» Why did Sam walk slowly? | Because he was looking for his shoes | Because he was tired and sleepy | *Because the floor was smooth and he might slide | Because the floor was sticky and hot
exercise: «The roads were slippy with ice, so the school bus was late.» Which word tells you why the roads were slippy? | bus | school | *ice | late
test: Ben says, «Watch out, the pavement is slippy!» What does he mean? | It is covered in paint | It is very hot to touch | *It is wet or smooth, so you could slip | It is clean and dry
test: Which word means the same as slippy but is more formal? | slow | *slippery | slap | sleepy
exam: What does slippy mean in «Mind the slippy steps in the rain»? | Very quiet | *Smooth or wet, so you slide | Very tall | Very clean
